# Copy to .env and fill in. POSTGRES_PASSWORD is required — compose fails
# rather than defaulting it (packaging-and-configuration.md §3).
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# POSTGRES_USER=verge
# POSTGRES_DB=verge
# Host address the web UI binds to. Defaults to 127.0.0.1 (loopback only).
# Set to 0.0.0.0, or a specific address, for direct host/LAN access.
# VERGE_BIND=127.0.0.1

# --- External database (docker-compose.external-db.yml) ---------------------
# Only read when you add the override:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.external-db.yml up -d
# Needs Docker Compose v2.24.0 or newer.
#
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD above is STILL REQUIRED in this mode, and nothing reads it.
# Compose interpolates the base file before it merges the override, so the base
# guard fires either way. Set it to a random throwaway value, not to a password
# you use anywhere (packaging-and-configuration.md §9.4).
#
# The DSN for your external Postgres. Required — compose fails rather than
# defaulting it. Do NOT put sslmode in it: an explicit DSN parameter overrides
# POSTGRES_SSLMODE below and silently turns verification off.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://verge:PASSWORD@db.example.com:5432/verge
#
# Path ON THE HOST to the CA root that signed your database's certificate — the
# anchor, not the server certificate. Required. It mounts read-only at
# /etc/verge/ca/root.crt. A path that does not exist fails `compose up` rather
# than creating an empty directory there.
# POSTGRES_SSLROOTCERT_SRC=/etc/ssl/certs/my-db-ca.crt
#
# Defaults to verify-full. The DSN host must appear in the server certificate's
# SAN. Lower it only knowingly.
# POSTGRES_SSLMODE=verify-full
